    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first team to reach 3000 points by melding sequences, creating canastas (7+ card sequences), and going out. Score points from melded cards plus bonuses for canastas.',
      "Turn-flow example: First player (to dealer's right) draws top card, decides to keep or discard it, then may meld and must discard. Play proceeds counter-clockwise. Each turn: draw from stock or take entire discard pile; optionally meld or add to team melds; discard one card. First player to empty hand takes a morto (11-card extra hand). Second morto goes to first player of other team who runs out. Team can end play with second batida if they have a clean canastra (7+ cards without wild).",
      'Scoring example: Scoring uses point values per card plus bonuses for canastras: clean (no wild) sequences of seven or more cards score 200 points, dirty sequences with a wild score 100 points, clean 13-card sequences score 500 points, clean 14-card sequences score 1000 points, and going out scores 100 points; card values from Pagat are added for melded cards and subtracted for cards left in hand, with penalties for unused mortos. First team to reach the target score (typically 3,000 points) wins; higher cumulative score wins..',
